# Agent worktrees: full embedded repo checkouts with their own node_modules.
# Exclude to keep the Docker build context small and avoid accidentally
# baking developer/agent state into the image.
.claude/
# Python bytecode and the pptx converter's per-deck scratch dirs never enter
# the image: the Dockerfile precompiles the converter itself, and `.build/` is
# output of `deck.sh check/build` (safe to delete, never an input).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.build/
# Build output of the dev/CI-only Open XML SDK validator (dotnet writes obj/
# next to the .csproj even when publishing elsewhere).
scripts/openxml-validator/bin/
scripts/openxml-validator/obj/
# The Open XML SDK validator source is dev/CI-only (run from the host checkout
# against produced decks), so it never belongs inside the image.
scripts/openxml-validator/

# Dev-only trees: never read at runtime or by the build (`npm run build` compiles
# src/ only). Excluding them keeps a docs- or tests-only commit a full cache hit.
docs/
tests/
# Deploy-host TLS material is bind-mounted at runtime (compose ./docker/tls →
# /app/tls:ro). It must never be baked into an image layer — a private key would
# ride every image copy — and a renewed cert would bust the app-layer cache.
docker/tls/
# pi-gateway (git submodule, included by docker-compose.yml): its own services build
# from it; none of it belongs in the Noah image.
vendor/pi-gateway/
